# Follow-up decision before validation measurements
GSE90070 Pmp22 chronic/control cytosolic log2 -2.934, polysome -3.505; late PERKi +2.740 and+3.272; relative loading +0.532. CPM retains direction. Chronic/acute RNA and polysome decline together, reproducing source-known congruence. New follow-up asks whether PERK inhibition is off-target versus pathway dependent. Prefer GSE49598 genetic PERK/eIF2alpha perturbation with same mouse fibroblast context, but changed ER stressor and duration. GSE118660 genetic PERK footprints hold Tg/context closer but n1/time/genotype and absent matched RNA limit inference. Both are more discriminating than another correlation screen. Primary genetic RNA criteria are sealed before either outcome acquisition. No assumption of clinical benefit: Pmp22 is dosage-sensitive and stress adaptation may differ from therapeutic normalization.
